  "Question": "What is the value of the following expression? \\[100(100-3)-(100 \\cdot 100-3)\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-20{,}000\\)",
    "B": "\\(-10{,}000\\)",
    "C": "\\(-297\\)",
    "D": "\\(-6\\)",
    "E": "\\(0\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Evaluate each parenthesized expression before taking the final difference. The first term is \\(100(100-3)=100\\cdot97=9700\\), and the second parenthesis is \\(100\\cdot100-3=10000-3=9997\\). Thus\n\\[\n100(100-3)-(100\\cdot100-3)\n=9700-9997=\\boxed{-297},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
